# Grouping arrives with the operator that made it unambiguous: `[f (x)]` is two
# elements only while juxtaposition means nothing, which is what an application
# operator settles. A group is a shape and not a step, so `(1)` reduces to `1` and
# a builtin inside one is still the function it names.
xs := ["a" "b"]

[
	(1)
	((xs |> @concat))
	(@concat <| xs)
	(@concat) <| xs
]
